{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory repeatedly recognized severe hypoxemia/respiratory failure risk, kept the patient in monitored oxygen-supported care, addressed refusal without allowing unsafe home observation, and converted family fatigue/conflict into executable bedside roles. It also actively corrected the recurrent misconception that “not intubated/not ICU” meant safe, used available system/record updates without overclaiming missing numbers, and maintained a safe open plan through the terminal family update. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is evident, and at least two high-order points were completed with meaningful trajectory impact, supporting grade 5.",
